    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d548-a1">

                <pb facs="0774" n="754" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg754"/>

                <head>Viscount Monck to Mr. Burnley.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Quebec,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 22, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 16th instant, covering a note from the Secretary of
                    State of the United States, in which he demands the extradition of certain
                    persons passing under the names, respectively, of Bell, Holt, Bristow, Robert
                    Drake, Burley, and Thomas.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to state, for the information of the Secretary of State of the
                    United States, that as soon as I shall have been advised that these persons, or
                    any of them, have been arrested in Canada, and that the proofs required by the
                    treaty shall have been made, the necessary warrants will be issued for their
                    delivery to the authorities of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MONCK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
